    <string name="m_hare_krishna_title">Hare Krishna Maha Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_hare_krishna_meaning">The great mantra for deliverance — a heartfelt call to Radha (Hare), Krishna and Rama to be engaged in loving devotion.</string>
    <string name="m_shiva_title">Om Namah Shivaya</string>
    <string name="m_shiva_meaning">“I bow to Shiva.” The five-syllable Panchakshara mantra, honouring the auspicious Self within all.</string>
    <string name="m_gayatri_title">Gayatri Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_gayatri_meaning">We meditate on the radiant divine light of Savitr; may it inspire and illumine our intellect.</string>
    <string name="m_mahamrityunjaya_title">Mahamrityunjaya Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_mahamrityunjaya_meaning">We worship the three-eyed Lord Shiva. As a ripe cucumber is freed from its vine, may we be freed from death — not from immortality.</string>
    <string name="m_vasudeva_title">Om Namo Bhagavate Vasudevaya</string>
    <string name="m_vasudeva_meaning">The twelve-syllable mantra: salutations to Lord Vasudeva (Krishna), the Supreme who dwells in all beings.</string>
    <string name="m_ram_title">Shri Ram Jai Ram</string>
    <string name="m_ram_meaning">The thirteen-syllable Rama mantra: victory to Lord Rama, the refuge of the devoted.</string>
    <string name="m_radhe_title">Radhe Radhe</string>
    <string name="m_radhe_meaning">The sweet name of Shri Radha, embodiment of pure love for Krishna, chanted throughout Vrindavan.</string>
    <string name="m_ganesha_title">Ganesha Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_ganesha_meaning">Salutations to Ganapati, remover of obstacles — chanted before every new beginning.</string>
    <string name="m_hanuman_title">Hanuman Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_hanuman_meaning">Salutations to Hanuman, giver of courage, strength and unwavering devotion.</string>
    <string name="m_narayana_title">Om Namo Narayanaya</string>
    <string name="m_narayana_meaning">The eight-syllable Ashtakshara mantra: salutations to Narayana, the eternal refuge of all beings.</string>
    <string name="m_saraswati_title">Saraswati Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_saraswati_meaning">Salutations to Saraswati, goddess of wisdom, speech, music and learning.</string>
    <string name="m_lakshmi_title">Lakshmi Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_lakshmi_meaning">Salutations to Mahalakshmi, goddess of abundance, prosperity and grace.</string>
    <string name="m_durga_title">Durga Mantra</string>
    <string name="m_durga_meaning">Salutations to Durga, the Divine Mother who protects her devotees from every difficulty.</string>
    <string name="m_om_title">Om (Pranava)</string>
    <string name="m_om_meaning">The primordial sound — the vibration of the Absolute from which all creation arises.</string>
